      "content": "Standardized tests are designed by predominantly white, middle-class test-makers who assume a narrow range of cultural experiences and knowledge, essentially creating a test that favors those who have had access to the same educational resources and cultural capital. This results in tests that are often opaque to non-English speakers, those from low-income backgrounds, and individuals from diverse cultural backgrounds, who may not have the same level of exposure to the dominant cultural references and knowledge that are embedded in the tests. As a result, these tests fail to accurately capture the cognitive abilities and potential of individuals from marginalized communities, instead perpetuating the myth that those who score well are inherently more intelligent or capable.",
